  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Winter Energy Needs Support by Conditional Cash Transfers for Vulnerable Frontline and Other Households in Zaporizhzhia and Donetska Oblasts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtWinter is a period of increased hardship for vulnerable&#xA0;front&#xA0;line communities. Russia&apos;s weaponisation of winter is expected to recommence. With the Ukrainian counter offensive underway and Russia attempting to halt advances, front line communities, especially those in key strategic and contested areas,&#xA0;are highly likely to have severely disrupted energy supplies during the winter months.&#xA0;lt/pgtltpgtThis project will support the solid fuel&#xA0;winter heating needs of 2,175&#xA0;vulnerable households (approximately 6,525&#xA0;direct beneficiaries)&#xA0;in 9 conflict-affected Hromadas (6 in Zaporizhzhia Oblast and 3 in Donetska Oblast). It will provide the selected HHs with&#xA0;solid fuel (coal, wood or&#xA0;sunflower briquettes)&#xA0;for 4 months (December&#xA0;2023 to March 2024).&#xA0;lt/pgtltpgtThe Shelter Cluster approved HH&#xA0;solid fuel requirements will be delivered &#xA0;through conditional cash transfers. This&#xA0;modality for the target front line Hromadas was agreed by the Shelter/ NFI&#xA0;Cluster (ltigtsee attached Cluster emaillt/igt)&#xA0;and the Local Government Authorities (ltigtsee attached request letterlt/igt).&#xA0;lt/pgtltpgtConditional cash will be provided&#xA0;by Dorcas (1,200 HH) and by&#xA0;local sub-partner City Aid Center (975 HH)&#xA0;through the selected beneficiaries&#xA0;UkrPostha (Ukrainian Post Office) accounts&#xA0;or local&#xA0;bank accounts.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
